Give a valid (feasible and efficient) solution very concisely. Use step1, step2, etc, and mention the tools to achieve each step. Use as few steps as possible and the answer should ideally be less than 100 words. When there is not a feasible solution given the constraint and provided tools, just say that it is not possible and give a very short justification.
A: Is the solution solvable? Please answer Yes or No.Yes.

To draw a circle and measure angles without a protractor or compass:

1. Tie the string around the drawing pin, leaving a small loop. (string)
2. Use the ruler to mark a point on the paper where you want the center of the circle to be. (ruler)
3. Place the drawing pin on the marked point, and use the string to create a small circle. (drawing pin, string)
4. To measure an angle, mark two points on the paper where the angle's sides meet. (pencil)
5. Place a drawing pin on each point, and use the ruler to measure the distance between them. (drawing pin, ruler)
6. Cut a piece of string to the measured length. (scissor, string)
7. Tie one end of the string to a fixed point, and the other end to a drawing pin at one of the marked points. (string, drawing pin)
8. Use a second drawing pin to hold the string taut against the paper, creating a right angle. (drawing pin)
9. Use the ruler to measure the distance from the fixed point to the second drawing pin. (ruler)
10. This distance will be the hypotenuse of a right triangle formed by the two sides of the angle. (pencil)
11. Since you know the length of the hypotenuse and one side, you can use the Pythagorean theorem to calculate the length of the other side. (pencil)
12. Now you can use the two sides to measure the angle using the cosine law or the sine law.
